      "content": "Subject: Prioritizing Your Health: Essential Ergonomics for Remote Work\n\nTo proactively support your well-being, please pay attention to your remote workstation ergonomics, as subtle discomforts can lead to real injuries over time. For instance, frequently slouching or tilting your neck even slightly strains the spine and muscles before you even notice pain. To prevent this, ensure your chair supports your lower back, your elbows rest at a 90-degree angle, and remember to implement standing or movement breaks regularly.",
